{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41159646",
      "title": "Working with Pages & Layouts",
      "lectureOrder": 90,
      "videoOrder": 84,
      "sourceHash": "764987b7bcb22533f138f2cfe8193676d8e26581f6e856add22cd162916ac912",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.02,
          "end": 2.61,
          "en": "Now, if you take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.61,
          "end": 6.21,
          "en": "at that starting project I prepared for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.21,
          "end": 9.51,
          "en": "you'll not just see that page JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.51,
          "end": 12.66,
          "en": "Instead, there also is a layout JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.66,
          "end": 15.563,
          "en": "and that's actually another reserved file name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.563,
          "end": 18.81,
          "en": "another special type of file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.81,
          "end": 22.98,
          "en": "where the page JS file defines the content of a page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.98,
          "end": 26.85,
          "en": "the layout JS file defines the shell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.85,
          "end": 29.73,
          "en": "around one or more pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.73,
          "end": 32.73,
          "en": "It's the, as the name implies, layout,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.73,
          "end": 34.713,
          "en": "into which a page will be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.7,
          "end": 37.53,
          "en": "And every next project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.53,
          "end": 41.46,
          "en": "needs at least one root layout JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.46,
          "end": 45.33,
          "en": "So, one layout JS file at the top of the app folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.33,
          "end": 48.6,
          "en": "You can also have nested layout JS files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.6,
          "end": 51.9,
          "en": "So, we could add one here in the about folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.9,
          "end": 55.32,
          "en": "and then this layout defined here would only apply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.32,
          "end": 57.72,
          "en": "to the pages in the about folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.72,
          "end": 60.36,
          "en": "and any nested folders there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.36,
          "end": 63.993,
          "en": "But you need at least one root layout JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.1,
          "end": 66.99,
          "en": "And as you can tell in that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.99,
          "end": 70.17,
          "en": "we're also exporting a React component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.17,
          "end": 72.543,
          "en": "just as we did it in that page file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.83,
          "end": 77.7,
          "en": "This component then uses the standard children prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.7,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "which in React can be used by every component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 84.99,
          "en": "to inject some content between the body tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.99,
          "end": 87.03,
          "en": "And that's also interesting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.03,
          "end": 92.03,
          "en": "This component actually renders an HTML and a body tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.19,
          "end": 95.61,
          "en": "So, some elements which you don't normally use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.61,
          "end": 97.8,
          "en": "in your React components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.8,
          "end": 101.43,
          "en": "but you actually need to do that in your next project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.43,
          "end": 103.02000000000001,
          "en": "in the root layout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.02000000000001,
          "end": 107.193,
          "en": "to set up the general HTML skeleton of the website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.50999999999999,
          "end": 112.02000000000001,
          "en": "Now, you might wonder where the head element is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.02000000000001,
          "end": 113.75999999999999,
          "en": "which is also typically needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.75999999999999,
          "end": 116.16,
          "en": "to set a title and some metadata,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.16,
          "end": 118.41,
          "en": "and that's actually not rendered here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.41,
          "end": 123.06,
          "en": "because that can be populated in a different way in NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.06,
          "end": 127.5,
          "en": "by exporting a special variable called metadata.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.5,
          "end": 129.96,
          "en": "Constant or variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.96,
          "end": 132.72,
          "en": "So, this is also a reserved name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.72,
          "end": 134.85,
          "en": "The component name was not reserved,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.85,
          "end": 137.37,
          "en": "but this here is a reserved name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.37,
          "end": 141.72,
          "en": "and if you export a variable or constant with that name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.72,
          "end": 143.94,
          "en": "it should contain an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.94,
          "end": 146.31,
          "en": "where you can then set the title of the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.31,
          "end": 148.2,
          "en": "and the description of the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.2,
          "end": 150.84,
          "en": "and also some other metadata fields,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.84,
          "end": 153.3,
          "en": "which will then applied to all pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.3,
          "end": 155.28300000000002,
          "en": "that are covered by that layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.27,
          "end": 158.57999999999998,
          "en": "So, that's why we don't have the head section here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.57999999999998,
          "end": 161.7,
          "en": "simply because all the content that goes into head",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.7,
          "end": 163.47,
          "en": "is set with that metadata,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.47,
          "end": 166.923,
          "en": "or automatically behind the scenes by NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.45,
          "end": 171.03,
          "en": "But what's now this children thing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.03,
          "end": 172.413,
          "en": "which is being output here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.43,
          "end": 176.64,
          "en": "Well, that will simply be the content of the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.64,
          "end": 178.29,
          "en": "that's currently active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.29,
          "end": 180.69,
          "en": "Because again, the layout is a wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.69,
          "end": 182.61,
          "en": "around one or more pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.61,
          "end": 184.68,
          "en": "and depending on which path you are,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.68,
          "end": 187.38,
          "en": "children will then simply be the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.38,
          "end": 190.203,
          "en": "of the page JS file that's currently active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.19,
          "end": 194.07,
          "en": "So, layout JS and page JS work together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.07,
          "end": 197.49,
          "en": "Layout is the wrapper, page is the actual content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.49,
          "end": 199.983,
          "en": "the content that will be injected here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
